(2426797, 335172, 35645, '<td valign="top">To explain the low score: I fail to see the lens cap - DNMC. The photo is very blurry (although the title suggests this is intentional). The photo is very small - there are tutorials on the site that explain resizing. There does not seem to be any particular subject to this photo other than the blurriness itself. <br/>Not trying to be mean, just explaining the vote.</td>', 'To explain the low score: I fail to see the lens cap - DNMC. The photo is very blurry (although the title suggests this is intentional). The photo is very small - there are tutorials on the site that explain resizing. There does not seem to be any particular subject to this photo other than the blurriness itself. Not trying to be mean, just explaining the vote.', '2006-05-17 18:35:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2426829, 332866, 35645, '<td valign="top">Not trying to be mean, just explaining the low vote: DNMC - no lens cap. <br/> <br/>Seems like this should have been in the environmental portrait challenge. If it had been, it would have gotten a 5 with this comment: this looks a little out of focus, perhaps due to being hand-held with a long-ish exposure. The vertical crop is a bit tight for my taste. The colors are great, and I like the diagonals made by the flutes(?). I like the intesity of the gaze, I just wish it were a little crisper.</td>', 'Not trying to be mean, just explaining the low vote: DNMC - no lens cap.  Seems like this should have been in the environmental portrait challenge. If it had been, it would have gotten a 5 with this comment: this looks a little out of focus, perhaps due to being hand-held with a long-ish exposure. The vertical crop is a bit tight for my taste. The colors are great, and I like the diagonals made by the flutes(?). I like the intesity of the gaze, I just wish it were a little crisper.', '2006-05-17 18:44:13.000000', NULL, 1),
