(2438014, 335564, 56454, '<td valign="top">Best of the pirates.  Details like stubble and the leather(?) vest help to separate it.  Great expression.  Nice lighting.  Why did all the pirates lose their right eyes?  Just curious.</td>', 'Best of the pirates.  Details like stubble and the leather(?) vest help to separate it.  Great expression.  Nice lighting.  Why did all the pirates lose their right eyes?  Just curious.', '2006-05-19 21:37:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2438020, 335562, 56454, '<td valign="top">Nice job.  I had a similar idea but couldn''t figure out how to do it.  <br/>It is by far the best of the pocket shots.  While I like color, I think BW was a good choice here.  Nice highlight lighting caught by the cap.  I would have liked to hear these model directions, "Okay, move your butt a little to the right. Too far!"</td>', 'Nice job.  I had a similar idea but couldn''t figure out how to do it.  It is by far the best of the pocket shots.  While I like color, I think BW was a good choice here.  Nice highlight lighting caught by the cap.  I would have liked to hear these model directions, "Okay, move your butt a little to the right. Too far!"', '2006-05-19 21:40:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2438033, 334109, 56454, '<td valign="top">And you shall get it!<br/> <br/>I''m generally not a fan of the toy pictures, maybe because I felt pretty beat up in the Children''s Toy Challenge. ;-)<br/> <br/>Franky, I''ve had a hard time rating this.  The scale works well between the the toy and the lens cap.  I also like the contrast between the smooth plastic and the rough brick.  I like how the DOF is up front and the focus fades as you move back.  Lighting is okay; not dramatic but good for picking up the textures.  Composition is pretty good too.  So, technically it is a solid photo.  Subject is still a struggle for me.</td>', 'And you shall get it! I''m generally not a fan of the toy pictures, maybe because I felt pretty beat up in the Children''s Toy Challenge. ;-) Franky, I''ve had a hard time rating this.  The scale works well between the the toy and the lens cap.  I also like the contrast between the smooth plastic and the rough brick.  I like how the DOF is up front and the focus fades as you move back.  Lighting is okay; not dramatic but good for picking up the textures.  Composition is pretty good too.  So, technically it is a solid photo.  Subject is still a struggle for me.', '2006-05-19 21:46:11.000000', NULL, 1),
