(2452197, 335071, 38218, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> Pretty good adaptation of an old "standby" (the martini glass). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Very true.  Unfortunately, that''s just a result of throwing this pic together at the last moment... no time to really fix it.</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: Pretty good adaptation of an old "standby" (the martini glass).   Very true.  Unfortunately, that''s just a result of throwing this pic together at the last moment... no time to really fix it.', '2006-05-24 07:15:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452199, 335071, 38218, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by amandalore:</b></div><hr/><i> creative!  I like the silver lens cap, maybe a less noisy background would help your photo out, also maybe dangle the string on the opposite side from shadow too... nice colors and good control on glass glare though </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for the tips, these are very helpful!</td>', 'Originally posted by amandalore: creative!  I like the silver lens cap, maybe a less noisy background would help your photo out, also maybe dangle the string on the opposite side from shadow too... nice colors and good control on glass glare though   Thank you for the tips, these are very helpful!', '2006-05-24 07:16:41.000000', NULL, 0),
