(2518338, 334936, 51538, '<td valign="top">This was too subtle to capture during the challenge.  But in retrospect, I think it is very well captured and presented.</td>', 'This was too subtle to capture during the challenge.  But in retrospect, I think it is very well captured and presented.', '2006-06-14 22:32:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2518889, 334170, 28710, '<td valign="top">Damned fine shot! Definitely underrated. Great choice of color for the background as it complements her eyes very well.<br/> <br/>A couple of things that might help:<br/> <br/>Try seeing how it looks to bring her away from the wall by a few feet. It might help to eliminate some shadows and make her ''pop'' a little more.<br/> <br/>Try pushing your exposure up just a hair (+1/3 stop?)<br/> <br/>Of course, I like the ''look up'' thing too.. There''s lots of hidden beauty in that suggestion...<br/> <br/>For tips on using adjustment layers, I learned a bucketload from www.radiantvista.com and their video tutorials... SO helpful! You will NEVER go back. Start with the big 130MB one..<br/> <br/>I then made an action to create all those layers for me and I just choose which one I want to play with... I usually do layers, curves for midtone contrast, curves for color casts and hue/saturation.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-15 00:31:31.</i></td>', 'Damned fine shot! Definitely underrated. Great choice of color for the background as it complements her eyes very well. A couple of things that might help: Try seeing how it looks to bring her away from the wall by a few feet. It might help to eliminate some shadows and make her ''pop'' a little more. Try pushing your exposure up just a hair (+1/3 stop?) Of course, I like the ''look up'' thing too.. There''s lots of hidden beauty in that suggestion... For tips on using adjustment layers, I learned a bucketload from www.radiantvista.com and their video tutorials... SO helpful! You will NEVER go back. Start with the big 130MB one.. I then made an action to create all those layers for me and I just choose which one I want to play with... I usually do layers, curves for midtone contrast, curves for color casts and hue/saturation.', '2006-06-15 01:30:44.000000', '2006-06-15 01:31:31.000000', 0),
(2522673, 334789, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Nice shot with very good DOF. <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Good Composition. The "son" is cut. Don''t know if it was possible to keep complete round of both lense caps.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>It was very tricky challenge. I actually could not think of any idea for this one. So nice take on the challenge.<br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Good DOF and colors. I would prefer more lights on the BG, particularly to bring out the beautiful building.<br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>More lights on the BG and full lense caps.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Nice over all shot, and deserves better score than what it got.<br/> <br/>Cheers!! Keep shooting.</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club. First Impression Nice shot with very good DOF. Composition: Good Composition. The "son" is cut. Don''t know if it was possible to keep complete round of both lense caps.Subject: It was very tricky challenge. I actually could not think of any idea for this one. So nice take on the challenge.Technical (Colour and light): Good DOF and colors. I would prefer more lights on the BG, particularly to bring out the beautiful building.Improvement: More lights on the BG and full lense caps.Summary: Nice over all shot, and deserves better score than what it got. Cheers!! Keep shooting.', '2006-06-16 14:35:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522739, 335597, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club. Sorry, I was off the hook for a while.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Like the idea, don''t like the execution. <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Composition is alright.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Fits the challenge.<br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Don''t think the border really goes with the picture. The lights on the lemon is blown out. When I look at the picture, my eyes first goes on the bright yellow border and then goes to the blown out area on the lemon.<br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>Border and blown out as mentioned above.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Not one of your great shot technically.<br/> <br/>Cheers!! Keep shooting.</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club. Sorry, I was off the hook for a while. First Impression Like the idea, don''t like the execution. Composition: Composition is alright.Subject: Fits the challenge.Technical (Colour and light): Don''t think the border really goes with the picture. The lights on the lemon is blown out. When I look at the picture, my eyes first goes on the bright yellow border and then goes to the blown out area on the lemon.Improvement: Border and blown out as mentioned above.Summary: Not one of your great shot technically. Cheers!! Keep shooting.', '2006-06-16 15:05:50.000000', NULL, 0),
